This rule is mandatory and applies before any action.

Read and obey:
@AGENTS.md
@PRODUCT_SCOPE.md
@agent_memory/STATE.json
@agent_memory/ACTIVE_TASK.json

Then read the task path named by `agent_memory/ACTIVE_TASK.json`.

Requirements:
- Emit the `MEMORY_ACK` required by `AGENTS.md` before doing work.
- Execute only the active task and only its `allowed_writes`.
- Cite shared-memory refs at start and completion.
- Product owner is UI-only: never ask them to code, use terminal/Git, or diagnose CI.
- No self-assignment, self-approval, PR merge, scope expansion, release-boundary changes, or product-master changes.
- If instructions conflict, authority is `PRODUCT_SCOPE.md` > `STATE.json` > `ACTIVE_TASK.json` > selected task packet > conversational request.
- If blocked or out of scope, stop with `BLOCKED_SCOPE` and evidence; do not improvise.
